Vendored schemas and edition manifests
--------------------------------------

Fifteen files under spec/ are copied verbatim from the Vortex repository
(https://github.com/vortex-data/vortex) at tag 0.86.1, commit d1fe2dc46d, and
remain under its license. Upstream paths are the ones that tag uses; several
moved afterwards, with byte-identical contents.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright the Vortex contributors

    spec/flatbuffers/dtype.fbs    vortex-flatbuffers/flatbuffers/vortex-dtype/dtype.fbs
    spec/flatbuffers/array.fbs    vortex-flatbuffers/flatbuffers/vortex-array/array.fbs
    spec/flatbuffers/layout.fbs   vortex-flatbuffers/flatbuffers/vortex-layout/layout.fbs
    spec/flatbuffers/footer.fbs   vortex-flatbuffers/flatbuffers/vortex-file/footer.fbs
    spec/proto/dtype.proto        vortex-proto/proto/dtype.proto
    spec/proto/scalar.proto       vortex-proto/proto/scalar.proto
    spec/proto/expr.proto         vortex-proto/proto/expr.proto
    spec/editions/*.toml          the frozen core edition manifests, as upstream's
                                  xtask generates them

The three pages and the refresh script beside them are this repository's own.
spec/METADATA.md in particular is a transcription, not a copy: the per-encoding
metadata messages are Rust structs upstream, with no schema file to vendor.


