Conformance corpus
------------------

tests/Vorticity.Conformance/corpus/ is generated, not copied. tools/conformance-gen
writes it by running the Vortex Rust library (Apache-2.0), and the data it feeds that
library comes from a splitmix64 stream whose master seed is recorded in the corpus
manifest along with the generator and upstream versions. No upstream file is
reproduced in it, and two runs of the generator produce identical bytes. It is
distributed under this repository's own Apache-2.0 license.


Zstandard
---------

src/Vorticity.Zstd is an independent implementation of the Zstandard format
(RFC 8878). Its decoding algorithms and its validation follow those of the
reference implementation, libzstd (https://github.com/facebook/zstd), so that
both accept and refuse the same frames. Its compressor reproduces libzstd's
compression parameters, match finders, block splitting and entropy coding, so
that both write the same frames; that part is derived from libzstd 1.5.7 and
remains under its license, quoted below.

The files under tests/Vorticity.Zstd.Tests/testdata/golden-* are copied verbatim
from the zstd repository at tag v1.5.7 (tests/golden-compression,
tests/golden-decompression, tests/golden-decompression-errors,
tests/golden-dictionaries) and remain under its license:

    Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates. All rights reserved.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0-only

tests/Vorticity.Zstd.Tests/testdata/decodecorpus/ is generated by zstd's
tests/decodecorpus.c (same license), built by tools/native-ref/build.sh; the
seeds are recorded in tools/native-ref/gen-decodecorpus.sh.

